(* Premise L2: "ring publish: a reader that acquires the head and fences
   reads the records' bytes the writer posted before its `fence w, w`"
   (planning/mvp-m8-plan.md, D-3 and D-9), a premise of P3 (ring safety),
   P4 (ring integrity), and P8 (drain) (planning/mvp-m8-specifications.md,
   sections 1 and 3, specification SHA-256
   ade32fa639d255ec2ba08040bbe8dbba2d7d8bf3fc4401947f4c542ecc9dc53d).
   Message passing with fence w,w and fence r,r on a ring, as compiled in
   build/mvp/gcc/be-mvp.elf and build/mvp/clang/be-mvp.elf (the lines in
   mvp/verify/litmus/sequences/SYMBOL-TOOLCHAIN.s; GCC's address, then
   Clang's): the outbound ring, which the domain hart writes and hart 0
   reads.
   P0, the domain hart in be_mvp_hart_main, posting READY and ENTERED:
     sb x6,0(x10)    READY's type byte, 1, be_mvp_ring_post (by store_le,
                     called at 102068516; inline)  1020682ee 102068a7e
     fence w,w       be_mvp_arch_fence_w_w, through be_mvp_exec_fence_w_w,
                     called at                          10206666e 10206676e
     sd x7,0(x11)    the head, 120, be_mvp_ring_publish 1020686a0 102068c20
   P1, hart 0 in drain:
     ld x5,0(x11)    the head, be_mvp_ring_acquire      1020686cc 102068c3e
     fence r,r       be_mvp_arch_fence_r_r, through be_mvp_exec_fence_r_r,
                     called at                          102064ad4 102065c62
     lbu x6,0(x10)   the type byte, be_mvp_ring_take (by load_le, called at
                     102068782; inline)                 10206830a 102068cf8
   Every writer posts, calls the same fence, then publishes, and every
   reader acquires, calls the fence, then takes; the excerpts list each
   call. The writers, in both ELFs: poll_input (the input ring); ping's
   PING and domain_failed's ACK (the inbound ring; GCC inlines both in
   drain); and on the outbound ring hart_fail's FAIL, console's LINE,
   ipi's PONG, stopped's SHUTDOWN (GCC inlines ipi and stopped in
   be_mvp_dispatch, Clang ipi alone), and be_mvp_hart_main's READY and
   ENTERED. The readers: drain (the outbound ring), acknowledged in
   hart_fail and ipi in be_mvp_dispatch (the inbound ring), console_read
   in be_mvp_dispatch (the input ring). Every other byte of the records is
   stored before the fence and loaded after it; the type byte stands for
   them. acquire's checks on the head branch before the fence, and a
   branch orders no later load under RVWMO (its rule 11 orders stores), so
   the test leaves them out. A reduced test keeps fewer accesses and
   orderings than the code, so it allows at least the code's outcomes:
   Never here is Never there.
   Forbidden: hart 0 reads the head of READY and ENTERED (80 and 40
   bytes) with the type byte as it was before READY's.
